From 5c5d2da0928fb9700a7d01f29238cf9e61621fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:39:35 +0000
Subject: Use the Bare mark for the launcher icon

The artwork fills the icon rather than sitting on a white circle: the design
lives entirely in the background layer with an empty foreground, since nothing
should float above a full bleed mark. The source disc is mapped onto the mask
circle so the mark is not cropped, and the gradient behind it is scaled well
past the corners so no mask shape can find a transparent one. Scaling costs
nothing there because the gradient is angular, so enlarging it changes coverage
and nothing else. Padding with a flat colour would not have worked: the
gradient's edge colour changes all the way round, and the join would have shown.

Both adaptive variants reference the same layers. They previously differed,
which is how one of them ended up cropped while the other looked correct.

The monochrome layer is a bitmap rather than a vector. Themed icons are
flattened to a single colour, so what is wanted is an alpha stencil, solid
across the mark with the ring punched out as transparency. As a vector that
could not be done: the mark's outline self-overlaps, evenOdd distorted it, and
a reverse wound circle only took the winding from two to one, leaving it filled.
A tintable bitmap gives the same result without fighting the path arithmetic.
